08:36:09 >>> show platform table ip
Stack member 1:

[Instance 0] 
+-----------------------Key-----------------------------------------------+
| IP address  =  Prefix within Longest Prefix Match table (SW)
| prefLen     =  Length of prefix within Longest Prefix Match table (SW)
| LTT         =  Lookup translation table entry (SW).
| REIdx       =  Route entry that prefix points to (SW).
| Route-Entry =  Action within route entry (RE-Idx). Displays:
|                Trap, drop or the MAC address retrived from the
|                fdb Index contained in route entry (HW).
| E     =  Encapsulation. (0=link layer, 1=tunnel) within route entry (HW).
| Dev   =  Instance Number in route entry (HW)
| Port  =  Front panel port number in route entry (HW)
| Tr    =  Trunk Id in route entry (HW)
| VID   =  Vlan ID in route Entry (HW)
| Mtu   =  Maximum transmit unit in route entry (SW)
| Ttl   =  Time To Live enabled/disabled  on route entry (HW)
| Cnt   =  Counter Set on route entry (HW)
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
See also:
show platform swtable FDBArp, InstanceMap, portMap.
show platform mem FdbIp, LPM, NextHopUnicast, Arp.


